  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Banco Internacional: Senior Loan to Support SME Portfolio in Ecuador</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project consists of providing Banco Internacional S.A. (&#x201c;Banco Internacional&#x201d; or the &#x201c;Bank&#x201d;) with a renewable senior A/B loan of up to US$100 million, structured as follows: (i) an A loan of up to US$50million to be funded by IDB Invest; and (ii) a B loan of up to US$50 million to be funded by other investors. The loan has a tenor of up to 3 years, with an option to renew for an additional three&#x2011;year period. The use of proceeds will support the growth of the Small and Medium-Sized Enterprises (&#x201c;SMEs&#x201d;) portfolio.Additionally, it is expected that the financing can be complemented with technical advisory services, defined jointly with Banco Internacional, to help strengthen its strategy and the development of its SMEs portfolio.</narrative>
  </description>
